    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core demand for Ameluz photodynamic therapy and RhodoLED lamp placements is growing, driving record product volumes and a sharp structural gross margin improvement after the company shifted from a high-cost transfer pricing model to a lower royalty-based sourcing arrangement. This lifts profitability and changes the earnings profile, but tight cash reserves create a significant liquidity overhang. The approval catalyst for a new Ameluz indication in basal cell carcinoma (PDUFA date September 2026) adds a major upside opportunity, leaving the operating story caught between strong commercial traction and financial fragility.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership transitioned the supply agreement to a direct royalty structure, which materially lowered cost of goods and underpins forward margin guidance. The team is advancing the regulatory filing for the BCC indication and signaling confidence in sustaining the new low-cost model. However, the lean cash position raises questions about the runway to potential revenue inflection without external financing. The recent analyst upgrade reflects improving earnings estimate momentum, lending some credibility to the margin narrative, while the liquidity burden remains a key execution risk.",
